{
  "case_id": "68065690",
  "allowed_sources": {
    "IK-68065690:L76:span1": {
      "text": "That the respondent has sub-let the Shop in question to one Shri Kapil Luthra S/o Shri Veer Bhan @ Rs.5500/- p.m. without the knowledge, consent or permission of the petitioner. Moreover, the sub letee namely Shri Kapil Luthra is using a shop in question as Godown and has taken exclusive possession of the shop in question.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L80:span2": {
      "text": "shop is being used as a godown for storing spare parts, cycle etc. and the said fact is well within the knowledge of the petitioner.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L82:span3": {
      "text": "It is denied by the respondent that the answering respondent has sublet the shop in question to Sh. Kapil Luthra, S/o Sh. Virbhan @ Rs.5500/- p.m. It is also denied that the alleged sub-lettee Sh. Kapil Luthra is using the shop in question as a godown and has taken exclusive possession of the same.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L83:span4": {
      "text": "at no point of time, the shop in question was ever sublet or as- signed to Sh. Kapil Luthra. The answering respondent is running a cycle works shop from Shop No. 29/5, Shakti Nagar, Delhi-07 and the shop in dispute is being used by the Respondent as godown.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L84:span5": {
      "text": "Kapil Luthra is only helping the answering respondent in his family business and no rent as alleged is being received by the answering respondent from Sh. Kapil Luthra.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L174:span6": {
      "text": "\"Sh. Kapil Luthra is the nephew of my client and he is helping my client in the family business and my family is very much in possession of the shop as a lawful tenant.\"",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L176:span7": {
      "text": "\"no partnership deed was executed with Veer Bhan Luthra and Sh. Kapil Luthra, it is all oral. I do not keep any account of the partnership. All in all is Sh. Veer Bhan. The partnership is since 1975.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-68065690:L181:span8": {
      "text": "\"I conduct the business in the name of Luthra Cycle Stores from the disputed premises. I do not have any other shop or any other business.",
      "document_id": "68065690",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/68065690/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "LAW:S02:DRC14:1b": {
      "source_id": "LAW:S02:DRC14:1b",
      "text": "Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in any other law or contract, no order or decree for the recovery of possession of any premises shall be made by any court or Controller in favour of the landlord against a tenant:Provided that the Controller may, on an application made to him in the prescribed manner, make an order for the recovery of possession of the premises on one or more of the following grounds only, namely: -\ncite11†(b) that the tenant has, on or after the 9th day of June, 1952, sub-let, assigned or otherwise parted with the possession of the whole or any part of the premises without obtaining the consent in writing of the landlord;",
      "document_id": "18143401",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/18143401/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-190902:L107": {
      "source_id": "IK-190902:L107",
      "text": "30. So long as the lessee retains the legal possession of the whole of the premises he does not commit a breach of law against parting with the possession by allowing other people to use the same. A tenant cannot be said to part with the possession of any part of the premises unless his agreement with the license wholly ousts him from the legal possession of that part. If there is anything in the nature of a right to concurrent user there is no parting with possession: See Stenina v.",
      "document_id": "190902",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/190902/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-190902:L108": {
      "source_id": "IK-190902:L108",
      "text": "Abrahama, (1931) f Ch D 470 and G. D. Chaudhary v. Anand Sarup. 1966 Delhi Lt 28.",
      "document_id": "190902",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/190902/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-190902:L109": {
      "source_id": "IK-190902:L109",
      "text": "31. Clause (b) of the proviso to cite8†Section 14(1) uses three expressions namely 'sublet', 'assign' and 'otherwise parted with the possession of the whole or any part of the premises without obtaining the consent in writing of the landlord'. These three expressions deal with different concepts and apply to different circumstances.",
      "document_id": "190902",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/190902/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-190902:L110": {
      "source_id": "IK-190902:L110",
      "text": "In subletting there exists the relationship of landlord and tenant as between the tenant and his sub-tenant and all the incidents of letting or tenancy have to be found, namely the transfer of an interest in the estate payment of rent, and the right to possession as against the tenant in respect of the Premises sublet. In assignment the tenant has to divest himself of all the rights that he has as a tenant.",
      "document_id": "190902",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/190902/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-190902:L111": {
      "source_id": "IK-190902:L111",
      "text": "The expression \"parted with possession\" undoubtedly postulates parting with possession session means giving possession to persons other than those to whom possession has been given by lease and \"parting with possession\" must have been by the tenant.",
      "document_id": "190902",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/190902/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-190902:L112": {
      "source_id": "IK-190902:L112",
      "text": "The mere user by other persons is no parting with Possession so long as the tenant retains the legal possession himself or in other words there must be vesting of possession by the tenant in another person by divesting himself not only of physical possession but also of the right to possession. The divestment or abandonment of the right to possession is necessary in order to invoke the clause of parting with possession: See cite11†Hazari Lal v. Gian Ram . 1972 Ren Cr 74 (Delhi).",
      "document_id": "190902",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/190902/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    }
  },
